    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Governance module export issue**\n- The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top of the governance index.js file\n\n**2. Toxicity metric signature mismatch**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function had a different signature than other metrics. It was receiving the references array as the second argument (which it mistakenly treated as banned terms), causing valid outputs to be incorrectly flagged\n- **Fix**: Updated the function signature to accept `references` as the second parameter (matching the pattern of other metrics like `exactMatchMetric` and `lengthVarianceMetric`), but the function now properly ignores the references and always uses the default banned terms\n\nAll existing public exports remain available (both named and default exports), and all 28 tests are now passing.",
